    "text": "The electric current through a wire varies with time as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The amount of electric charge crossed through a section of the wire in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> is:",
